# DO NOT USE. Kept only as a record of an experiment (see docs/investigation.md section 4).
# A 5 s SCSI command timeout for the DS-SC5B bridges (174c:55aa) was tried before the arbiter
# existed. It is not needed with uas_arb, and it breaks disk spin-down: a sleeping drive takes
# ~15 s to spin up, so every spin-up hits the 5 s timeout and causes aborts + a USB reset.
# Leave the Linux default (30 s).
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="scsi", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="scsi_device", ATTRS{idVendor}=="174c", ATTRS{idProduct}=="55aa", ATTR{timeout}="5"
